Consider, for a moment, that it is not just protection that
gray/black/silver dragon scales and mail provide, but *certain*
protection.

Wear silver armor, and ray effects - most importantly wands of death -
*never* work.  Wear BDSM and disintegration attacks *never* harm your
person.  Wear gray dragon armor, and Touch Of Death spells *never*
instantly kill you.

These armor types are so popular because they defend against
instadeaths.  Not ordinary ones either, like drawbridge things that
can be prepared against with experience, or chowing down on Leg of
Cockatrice, but those that resort from attacks.  That makes these
things the most important element of any ascension kit, especially
since the Wizard uses Touch of Death, Black Dragons are not infrequent
in lower levels and can attack from a distance, and any intelligent
monster that happens upon a wand of death will pick it up and use it.

There are other defenses against all of these things; high AC already
makes wands and dragon breath less likely to hit, and you get a saving
throw against Touch of Death.  But the more times opponents use these
things, the greater the chance they'll get lucky.  There's a chance
they'll get lucky the first time, even.

Thus, I predict that most people will eschew multi-colored dragon
armor in favor of the traditional defenses.  An ascension-worthy game
is too precious a commodity to take half-measures with.  (Well, to me
anyhow.)

